        </div>

        <h1 class="docs-title">RotaryCAM vs. <span class="text-gradient-amber">Hypertherm ProNest</span></h1>
        <p class="docs-subtitle">
          Hypertherm ProNest and ProNest LT set the industrial bar for high-volume plate nesting and SureCut automation. If your shop runs a 4-axis rotary tube table or mixed custom CNC plasma setup, here is how the two tools compare.
        </p>

        <div class="docs-meta-bar">
          <span class="docs-meta-pill amber"><strong>Comparison</strong> &bull; Enterprise Plate CAM vs. 4-Axis Tube &amp; Sheet CAM</span>
          <span class="docs-meta-pill cyan"><strong>OS Support:</strong> macOS, Windows &amp; Linux (Offline)</span>
          <span class="docs-meta-pill"><strong>Pricing:</strong> $199 Maker / $399 Pro Shop Perpetual</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="container docs-shell">
      <aside class="docs-sidebar" aria-label="Comparison Navigation">
        <div class="docs-sidebar-group">
          <div class="docs-sidebar-heading">On This Page</div>
          <ul class="docs-toc-list">
            <li><a href="#matrix"><span class="docs-toc-step">01</span><span>Side-by-Side Specs</span></a></li>
            <li><a href="#differences"><span class="docs-toc-step">02</span><span>Where They Diverge</span></a></li>
            <li><a href="#when-to-choose"><span class="docs-toc-step">03</span><span>When to Choose Which</span></a></li>
            <li><a href="#faq"><span class="docs-toc-step">04</span><span>Fabricator FAQ</span></a></li>
            <li><a href="#try-offline"><span class="docs-toc-step">05</span><span>Test on Your Parts</span></a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="docs-sidebar-group">
          <div class="docs-sidebar-heading">Other Comparisons</div>
          <ul class="docs-nav-list">
            <li>
              <a href="{{ root_prefix }}compare/sheetcam/">
                <span class="docs-nav-num">VS</span>
                <span>SheetCAM + Rotary</span>
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="{{ root_prefix }}compare/pronest/" class="active">
                <span class="docs-nav-num">VS</span>
                <span>Hypertherm ProNest</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </aside>

      <div class="docs-main">
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="matrix">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">01 &bull; Specs</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Side-by-Side Comparison</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              ProNest is engineered for industrial plate production centers. RotaryCAM is engineered from the ground up for 4-axis rotary tube, structural profiles, and flat sheet in a single offline app.
            </p>
            <div class="table-wrap">
              <table class="doc-table">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>Capability</th>
                    <th>Hypertherm ProNest / ProNest LT</th>
                    <th>RotaryCAM</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td><strong>Core Focus</strong></td>
                    <td>High-volume 2D industrial plate nesting, multi-torch tables, and ERP/MRP automation</td>
                    <td>4-axis rotary pipe, HSS, structural steel, and 2D flat-sheet CAM in one desktop app</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><strong>3D Tube &amp; Structural Import</strong></td>
                    <td>Requires separate rotary/tube CAD/CAM modules and higher product tiers</td>
                    <td>Built-in 3D STEP/IGES import for pipe, HSS, angle iron, C-channel, I-beam, and bent sticks</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><strong>Hole &amp; Bevel Automation</strong></td>
                    <td>Proprietary SureCut True Hole, Rapid Part, and multi-axis bevel head support</td>
                    <td>Zero-bevel saddle pullback on perpendicular torches, 60% small-hole rules, tabs, and 4-axis eccentric weld bevels</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><strong>Controllers Supported</strong></td>
                    <td>Optimized for Hypertherm CNCs/XPR/MAXPRO/Powermax and industrial production tables</td>
                    <td>14 hobby-to-industrial dialects (SimCNC, LinuxCNC QTPlasmaC, Mach3/4, MASSO, Acorn, FireControl, FlashCut, EdingCNC, UCCNC, WinCNC, PlanetCNC, grblHAL, Generic G94)</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><strong>1D &amp; 2D Nesting</strong></td>
                    <td>Enterprise automated 2D plate nesting, remnant tracking, and ERP quoting (ProNest)</td>
                    <td>1D multi-stick tube nesting (180&deg; flips, A-rolls, common-line severs) + 2D plate cutout nesting and guillotine crops</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><strong>Cut Charts</strong></td>
                    <td>Built-in Hypertherm SureCut process database</td>
                    <td>1,025 built-in presets (Hypertherm SYNC, Duramax, Air Plasma) + unit-aware CSV import/export</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><strong>Operating Systems</strong></td>
                    <td>Windows</td>
                    <td>Native macOS, Windows, and Linux (100% air-gapped offline)</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><strong>Pricing &amp; Licensing</strong></td>
                    <td>ProNest LT subscription (~$60/mo or $500+/yr) or enterprise ProNest licensing + modules</td>
                    <td>30-day free beta; Maker $199 USD / Pro Shop $399 USD perpetual offline key (optional $59/$99/yr updates)</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="doc-step-card" id="differences">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">02 &bull; Architecture</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Where the Two Products Diverge</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <div class="compare-feature-grid">
              <div class="compare-feature-box">
                <h3>Rotary &amp; Structural Included Out of the Box</h3>
                <p>
                  Instead of bolting separate pipe modules onto a plate nest engine, RotaryCAM parses 3D STEP assemblies natively for round pipe, square/rect HSS, angle iron, C-channel, I-beam, and cut-and-bend tubes.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="compare-feature-box">
                <h3>Hobby-to-Industrial Controller Coverage</h3>
                <p>
                  Small fab shops and custom table builders rarely run factory Hypertherm CNC consoles. RotaryCAM generates native G93, G94, and SimCNC 4D trajectory G-code for 14 controller dialects right out of the box.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="compare-feature-box">
                <h3>Zero-Bevel Fit-Up on a Standard Torch</h3>
                <p>
                  Without a 5-axis bevel head, steep saddle intersections leave an overhanging inner edge. RotaryCAM computes the inner-wall intersection curve and clamps the cut path so coped tubes mate tight.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="compare-feature-box">
                <h3>Perpetual Offline Ownership</h3>
                <p>
                  Activate with a local `rotarycam.lic` file on Mac, Windows, or Linux. There is no mandatory cloud login, no seat-lease timeout if shop Wi-Fi drops, and no recurring subscription required to keep cutting.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="doc-step-card" id="when-to-choose">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">03 &bull; Honest Fit</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">When to Choose ProNest vs. RotaryCAM</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              Enterprise plate CAM and agile 4-axis tube CAM solve different shop bottlenecks. Choose based on your floor hardware and order volume.
            </p>
            <div class="compare-verdict-grid">
              <div class="compare-card competitor">
                <div class="compare-card-kicker">Best Fit For High-Volume Industrial Plate</div>
                <h3>Choose Hypertherm ProNest / ProNest LT if:</h3>
                <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
                  <li><strong>You run Hypertherm XPR, MAXPRO, or HPR tables</strong> and need certified SureCut True Hole, Rapid Part, and multi-head bevel automation.</li>
                  <li><strong>Your production team relies on ERP/MRP integration</strong>, automated job quoting, remnant databases, and multi-shift plate scheduling.</li>
                  <li><strong>Your work is predominantly heavy 2D plate cutting</strong> on Windows with an enterprise software budget.</li>
                </ul>
              </div>

              <div class="compare-card rotarycam">
                <div class="compare-card-kicker">Best Fit For Tube, Structural &amp; Custom Fab Shops</div>
                <h3>Choose RotaryCAM if:</h3>
                <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
                  <li><strong>You fabricate handrails, roll cages, trailers, or structural frames</strong> from round pipe, HSS, angle iron, channel, or I-beam alongside flat brackets.</li>
                  <li><strong>You run SimCNC, LinuxCNC QTPlasmaC, MASSO, Acorn, Mach3/4, WinCNC, or FireControl</strong> and want dialed-in 4-axis rotary + 2D G-code without module upsells.</li>
                  <li><strong>You prefer a fast offline app</strong> on macOS, Windows, or Linux with one-time $199/$399 perpetual pricing.</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="doc-step-card" id="faq">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">04 &bull; FAQ</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Common Fabricator Questions</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <div class="compare-faq-list">
              <div class="compare-faq-item">
                <h3>Does RotaryCAM require a Hypertherm plasma cutter or Hypertherm CNC controller?</h3>
                <p>
                  No. It ships with 1,025 presets covering Hypertherm SYNC, Hypertherm Duramax, and Generic Air Plasma torches (plus CSV chart import/export), and outputs native G-code for 14 popular hobby-to-industrial controllers.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="compare-faq-item">
                <h3>Can RotaryCAM import multi-part 3D STEP assemblies without extra add-on modules?</h3>
                <p>
                  Yes. Multi-body `.step`/`.stp` inspection, profile autodetection, cut-and-bend unfolding, and 4-axis kinematics are built directly into the core desktop app.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="compare-faq-item">
                <h3>How does RotaryCAM handle small holes and edge quality compared to industrial CAM?</h3>
                <p>
                  RotaryCAM applies 60% small-hole speed reduction, synchronous `M62/M63` THC void locking, overburn prevention, kerf-compensated tabs, and zero-bevel fishmouth compensation.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="compare-faq-item">
                <h3>Is RotaryCAM a monthly subscription like ProNest LT?</h3>
                <p>
                  No. Maker ($199) and Pro Shop ($399) are perpetual offline licenses with 1 year of updates included. Optional renewals ($59/$99/yr) are only needed if you choose to upgrade in Year 2 or later.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="compare-faq-item">
                <h3>Can I test RotaryCAM on my own STEP and DXF files before buying?</h3>
                <p>
                  Yes. Download the free 30-day offline beta and test your real `.step`, `.dxf`, and `.svg` parts in the 3D simulator with your controller's post output.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <div class="compare-cta-box" id="try-offline">
          <div class="compare-cta-copy">
            <h2>Test Your Own STEP and DXF Parts Free for 30 Days</h2>
            <p>
              Run RotaryCAM offline on macOS, Windows, or Linux. Drop a tube frame STEP assembly or bracket DXF kit in and inspect every pierce, lead-in, and G93/G94 feedrate line in 3D.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="compare-cta-actions">
            <a href="{{ root_prefix }}index.html#download" class="compare-btn-primary">Download 30-Day Beta &rarr;</a>
            <a href="{{ docs_prefix }}index.html" class="compare-btn-secondary">Browse 13 Guides</a>
          </div>
        </div>

